From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:30:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] KaplanSurrogateLUT: store full cascade outcomes
 (individual re-emitted phonons)

The surrogate stored per (energy, quantile) only the absorbed fraction and the
SUM of re-emitted phonon energy, and re-emitted that sum as a single phonon.
Re-emitted Kaplan phonons are mostly sub-gap; merged into one phonon above 2D
they break pairs again on re-entry, so the collected-energy fraction in a
cavity with return probability 0.9 was +13% (15-35 D) too high; the table also
used the lower energy node only (+10% at 3 D) and clamped above 40 D.
Now each of 128 energy nodes keeps 512 complete KaplanFilm::absorb_phonon
outcomes (absorbed fraction + list of re-emitted fractions); lookup picks one
of the two bracketing nodes with linear-interpolation probability and falls
back to the full cascade outside [2 D, 40 D]. Surrogate/full agreement is now
< 1% (tests/test_kaplan). Kaplan cascade per Kaplan et al. PRB 14, 4854 (1976);
eta_pb checks vs campaign WP5-v4 (W13) and 1401.1937 [FT] in the same test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BcNoovRae5kkbL36KL3sYy
